{
  "schema_version": "1",
  "description": "Per-fund facts that Form N-PORT does not carry: net and gross expense ratio, inception, tracked index and stated mandate. Read from each sponsor's own prospectus, SAI or fund page and committed with a URL and a date, because a fee or an index can change and a number without a date cannot be rechecked. This file is an INPUT to the screen, not an output of it, and it contains no price, return or performance data of any kind.",
  "date_read": "2026-08-12",
  "mandate_change_policy": {
    "tier_1_excluded": "A fund whose STATED INVESTMENT OBJECTIVE OR MANDATE changed inside the observation window is given the reserved mandate 'mandate_changed', which is absent from the predeclared intended-factor map and therefore fails the screen. It is recorded with its change date rather than silently dropped. The reason is not that such a fund is bad: it is that it has no single stated mandate over the window, so there is nothing to grade its exposure against.",
    "tier_2_retained_and_reported": "A change of tracked index, index name or index methodology that leaves the stated mandate intact does NOT exclude a fund. Excluding those would remove most of the shelf and would hide exactly what the rolling-loading stability test exists to find. Every one is recorded below and reported beside the stability results."
  },
