  "securities_lending": {
    "note": "Whatever a fund keeps from lending is already inside net asset value and therefore already inside every return in this experiment; it is recorded here as a product fact, not added to anything. The four disclosures below use DIFFERENT DENOMINATORS and must never be put in one column: iShares' 81% excludes collateral investment fees, SPDR's 85% is of net proceeds after borrower rebates, Vanguard has no split at all, and Invesco states no ratio.",
    "Vanguard": {
      "split": "none; the SAI reports $0 of fees paid to a lending agent from a revenue split. Vanguard self-lends and charges administration and cash-collateral-management fees directly.",
      "as_of": "FY ended 2025-12-31",
      "source_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/36405/000003640526000181/f45032d1.htm"
    },
    "iShares/BlackRock": {
      "split": "the fund retains 81% of securities lending income excluding collateral investment fees, never less than 70% of lending income plus collateral investment fees, stepping to 84% above a complex-wide annual threshold. The agent is an affiliate.",
      "as_of": "FY ended 2026-03-31",
      "source_url": "https://www.ishares.com/us/literature/annual-financial-statements/afs-b-ishares-core-s-and-p-etfs-03-31-en.pdf"
    },
    "State Street SPDR": {
      "split": "the fund retains 85% of NET proceeds after borrower rebates, 15% to State Street; 90/10 above a threshold. The agent is an affiliate.",
      "as_of": "FY ended 2025-06-30",
      "source_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1064642/000119312525197943/d941109dncsr.htm"
    },
    "Invesco": {
      "split": "UNVERIFIED. Invesco discloses dollars only and states no ratio anywhere findable; the fund's share of GROSS derived from those tables is roughly 2-3%, because borrower rebates dominate, which is a different quantity from an agent split.",
      "as_of": "FY ended 2025-04-30",
      "source_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1209466/000110465925084008/tm2522887d1_485bpos.htm"
    }
  },
  "unverified": [
    "Vanguard's index PROVIDER entity is unverified: the 2026-07-29 supplement renames the indexes to Morningstar after Morningstar acquired CRSP, but the April 2026 prospectus trademark page still names Center for Research in Security Prices, LLC as licensor. The index NAMES are verified; which legal entity now licenses and calculates them is not.",
    "IJK's expense ratio is 0.17 on the 2026-06-30 fact sheet and 0.16 in the 2026-07-31 prospectus and on the live page. 0.16 is used.",
    "Invesco's securities-lending revenue split, as above.",
    "The State Street 2025 name-prefix rebrand has no dedicated 497 and its effective date is unverified. Tickers, indexes, objectives and expense ratios are unchanged.",
    "A 2023-05-26 Vanguard board approval to move VTI, VOO, VB and VO into different trusts appears never to have been effected; no withdrawal supplement was found, so the cancellation is inferred rather than documented.",
    "SPYG's inception date is not in its summary prospectus and comes from the SSGA product page.",
    "RPG's and FTC's inception dates are the 'Inception Date' column of the prospectus performance table rather than a separate statement.",
    "The nature and effective date of the FTC/FTA base-index change of 2023-12-01, as above."
  ],
  "access_notes": [
    "ishares.com returns HTTP 403 to a plain client and is served normally to curl with a browser agent; invesco.com returns HTTP 406 to curl, so PDP and SPHQ come from EDGAR; wisdomtree.com, jhinvestments.com return 403 and principalam.com/us/etf/USMC returns 404, so EZM, JHMM and USMC come from EDGAR.",
    "Vanguard fund pages are JavaScript shells. Inception dates come from Vanguard's own JSON profile API because they appear in neither the prospectus nor the SAI."
  ],
